Host Plugin Interface + Effect Spec: The Equalizer
Version: 1.0
Goal: A drop-in Python plugin module discoverable by host.py. Another implementer
should be able to reproduce this 10-band graphic equalizer if they obey this
interface and the DSP rules below.

==============================================================================
1. DISCOVERY
==============================================================================
The host imports Python modules and treats a module as a plugin if it defines a
class that exposes ALL of:
  get_name(self) -> str
  get_knobs(self) -> List[Knob]
  get_switches(self) -> List[Switch]
  apply_effect(self, audio, sample_rate: int)

Optional but recommended:
  get_colors(self) -> dict[str, str]

The plugin class is instantiated once (or once per chain slot). The instance is
long-lived. The host mutates instance attributes, then calls apply_effect.

Suggested class name: TheEqualizer
Suggested module name: the_equalizer.py

==============================================================================
2. SHARED DATACLASSES
==============================================================================
Must exist in the plugin module OR be imported from the host’s identical
definitions.

from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from typing import List

@dataclass
class KnobColorScheme:
    outline: str = "black"
    face: str = "white"
    needle: str = "black"

@dataclass
class Knob:
    name: str = "Generic"
    min: float = 0.0
    max: float = 1.0
    default: float = 0.5
    click_pts: List[float] = field(default_factory=lambda: [0.5])
    knob_color_scheme: KnobColorScheme = field(
        default_factory=lambda: KnobColorScheme(
            outline="black", face="white", needle="black"
        )
    )

@dataclass
class Switch:
    name: str = "Enable"
    default: bool = True

Rules:
  - Knob.name and Switch.name are UI labels AND the source of the live
    attribute name (see §4).
  - min < max. default must lie in [min, max].
  - click_pts are suggested detent values; they do not change the continuous
    range unless the host snaps.
  - Colors are CSS hex or CSS color names.

==============================================================================
3. REQUIRED METHODS
==============================================================================
get_name()
  Must return exactly: "The Equalizer"

get_knobs()
  Returns the full ordered list of knobs. Order is display order (left-to-right
  / low-to-high frequency). Called at UI build time; do not change the list
  later unless the host rebuilds.

get_switches()
  Returns the full ordered list of boolean switches. First switch is Enable.

get_colors()  [required for this skin]
  Returns a dict used by the host skin. Keys (all CSS colors / hex strings):
    face, edge, text, muted,
    button, button_hot, button_on, button_text,
    switch_on, switch_off,
    slider, slider_handle,
    knob_outline, knob_face, knob_needle

apply_effect(audio, sample_rate: int)
  audio: NumPy array float-like in [-1, 1], shape (n,) or (n, channels)
         Some hosts may pass (channels, n) with a small channel axis; detect
         and preserve the input layout on output.
  sample_rate: int Hz
  MUST return a NumPy array:
    - same length n along the time axis
    - same number of dimensions and channel count as input
    - finite values
  MUST be safe for audio == empty or None (return empty float array).
  MUST NOT assume extra keyword arguments; all parameters come from instance
  attributes.
  MUST honor Enable bypass: if the enable attribute is False / 0 / "false" /
  "off", return audio unchanged.
  MUST NOT print, do file I/O, or open a GUI inside apply_effect.
  Do not change sample_rate. Do not return int PCM.
  Input may be float32 or float64; returning float32 is acceptable if input
  was float32.

==============================================================================
4. LIVE PARAMETER BINDING (critical)
==============================================================================
The host does NOT call apply_effect(hz31=...). It writes fields onto the
instance first.

Binding rule:
  attribute_name = knob_or_switch.name.strip().lower()
  with spaces and hyphens removed.

IMPORTANT: attribute names MUST be valid Python identifiers and MUST NOT
start with a digit. Names like "31 Hz" -> "31hz" will silently fail on many
hosts, leaving every band at 0 dB (no audible change). Use letter-prefixed
knob names as specified in §5.

Implementers MUST initialize these attributes in __init__ to the same defaults
advertised by get_knobs / get_switches so apply_effect works before the GUI
moves anything.

Inside apply_effect, read with getattr(self, name, default) and/or self.__dict__
so a partial host cannot crash the plugin. Clip each gain to [min, max].

Required live attributes and defaults:
  self.name    = "The Equalizer"
  self.enable  = True
  self.hz31    = 0.0
  self.hz62    = 0.0
  self.hz125   = 0.0
  self.hz250   = 0.0
  self.hz500   = 0.0
  self.hz1k    = 0.0
  self.hz2k    = 0.0
  self.hz4k    = 0.0
  self.hz8k    = 0.0
  self.hz16k   = 0.0

==============================================================================
5. KNOB / SWITCH DEFINITIONS
==============================================================================
Ten gain knobs, in this exact order. Units are decibels.

Knob "Hz31"   min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=31 Hz
Knob "Hz62"   min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=62 Hz
Knob "Hz125"  min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=125 Hz
Knob "Hz250"  min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=250 Hz
Knob "Hz500"  min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=500 Hz
Knob "Hz1k"   min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=1000 Hz
Knob "Hz2k"   min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=2000 Hz
Knob "Hz4k"   min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=4000 Hz
Knob "Hz8k"   min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=8000 Hz
Knob "Hz16k"  min=-12 max=12 default=0.0  click_pts=[-12,-6,-3,0,3,6,12]   fc=16000 Hz

Switch "Enable" default True

KnobColorScheme for ALL knobs (required look):
  outline = "black"
  face    = "silver"
  needle  = "black"

Required get_colors palette (bright yellow face, dark controls):
  face="#FFD400"
  edge="#111111"
  text="#111111"
  muted="#5a5a5a"
  button="#222222"
  button_hot="#333333"
  button_on="#111111"
  button_text="#FFD400"
  switch_on="#111111"
  switch_off="#888888"
  slider="#222222"
  slider_handle="#C0C0C0"
  knob_outline="black"
  knob_face="silver"
  knob_needle="black"

==============================================================================
6. DSP SPECIFICATION
==============================================================================
Effect type: 10-band graphic equalizer.
Each band is a peaking (bell) EQ at the center frequency in §5.

Band Q: 2.0  (about 2/3–1 octave; clearly audible when a knob is moved).

Skip a band if abs(gain_db) < 0.05 (treat as flat).
If ALL bands are flat OR enable is off, return the input buffer unchanged.

Nyquist guard:
  sr = max(int(sample_rate) or 44100, 8000)
  fc_used = min(band_fc, 0.45 * sr)
  If fc_used < 20 Hz, skip that band.

Peaking biquad (RBJ cookbook), one SOS section per active band:

  A     = 10 ** (gain_db / 40)
  w0    = 2 * pi * fc_used / sr
  alpha = sin(w0) / (2 * Q)
  b0 =  1 + alpha * A
  b1 = -2 * cos(w0)
  b2 =  1 - alpha * A
  a0 =  1 + alpha / A
  a1 = -2 * cos(w0)
  a2 =  1 - alpha / A
  sos = [[b0/a0, b1/a0, b2/a0, 1.0, a1/a0, a2/a0]]

Cascade active sections in band order (low to high).
Process each channel independently.

If scipy is available:
  use scipy.signal.sosfilt with sosfilt_zi, keeping per-section per-channel
  filter state on the instance so consecutive buffers are continuous.

If scipy is not available:
  implement direct-form II on each section and keep two delay states
  (w1, w2) per section per channel on the instance.

When any gain, set of active bands, or sample_rate changes, rebuild SOS
coefficients and reset stored filter state.

After filtering, clip samples to [-1, 1].

Internal caches keyed by (sample_rate, rounded gains) are allowed.
Assume the host calls apply_effect from one thread at a time.

==============================================================================
7. APPLY_EFFECT I/O RULES
==============================================================================
- Do not change sample_rate.
- Do not return a longer or shorter buffer than the input time length.
- Preserve channel count and layout.
- Must be re-entrant per instance: consecutive calls use current attributes.
- No extra kwargs. No prints. No file I/O. No GUI.

==============================================================================
