==============================================================================
class TheEqualizer:
    def __init__(self):
        # set name, enable, hz31..hz16k defaults
    def get_name(self) -> str:
        # "The Equalizer"
    def get_colors(self):
        # yellow-face palette above
    def get_knobs(self) -> List[Knob]:
        # 10 knobs Hz31..Hz16k
    def get_switches(self) -> List[Switch]:
        # Enable
    def apply_effect(self, audio, sample_rate: int):
        # bypass / 10 peaking bands / same shape out

==============================================================================
9. ACCEPTANCE CHECKS
==============================================================================
- Host can discover the class via the four required methods.
- get_name() == "The Equalizer"
- Face color is bright yellow (#FFD400). Knobs are black outline, silver face,
  black needle.
- Moving Hz1k to +12 dB on music or noise produces an obvious mid boost.
- Moving Hz1k to -12 dB produces an obvious mid cut.
- All knobs at 0 dB returns audio unchanged (within numerical noise).
- enable=False returns audio unchanged even if knobs are not zero.
- Empty input does not raise.
- Output length and channel count match input.
- Attribute names are hz31, hz62, hz125, hz250, hz500, hz1k, hz2k, hz4k,
  hz8k, hz16k, enable — all valid Python identifiers.